          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "প্রভাব (prôbhāb) is Sanskrit prabhāva, might or power (Monier-Williams). The Bengali sense, the pull one thing has on another, is a softening of that power; the influence falls on something, so it goes with -এর ওপর."
            }
          ]
        },
